[TEST 1/3] Fused SwiGLU Backward Elementwise Kernel (Pre-Training & SFT)
  - Workload Shape      : [M=2048, H=5504]
  - Vectorization       : 128-bit uint4 (8 halfs / 16 bytes per thread)
  - d_gate Max Abs Diff : 9.765625e-04 (Tolerance: < 2e-3) -> PASS
  - d_up Max Abs Diff   : 9.765625e-04 (Tolerance: < 2e-3) -> PASS
  - Measured Latency    : 0.460 ms (200 timed reps with CUDA Events)
  - Effective Bandwidth : 244.8 GB/s (76.5% of Tesla T4 320 GB/s Peak DRAM Roofline)

[TEST 2/3] Fused SFT LoRA Backward + Inline AdamW Optimizer Kernel (Fine-Tuning)
  - Workload Shape      : [M=1024, d_in=2048, d_out=2048, r=32]
  - Mechanism           : Fuses dB accumulation, AdamW update on B, dH backpropagation, 
                          dA accumulation, AdamW update on A, and dX backpropagation into 
                          a streamlined kernel pipeline with zero intermediate VRAM roundtrips.
  - dX Backprop Diff    : 1.525879e-05 (Tolerance: < 5e-3) -> PASS
  - Adapter A Diff      : 6.047245e-04 (Tolerance: < 1e-3) -> PASS
  - Adapter B Diff      : 3.647525e-05 (Tolerance: < 1e-4) -> PASS
  - AdamW Momentum Diff : 5.215406e-08 (Tolerance: < 1e-5) -> PASS
  - Measured Latency    : 2.289 ms (Single Fused Kernel Launch) -> PASS

[TEST 3/3] Pre-Training Dense Fused Backward GEMM + Inline AdamW Kernel (H6)
  - Workload Shape      : [M=2048, N=2048, K=1024]
  - Mechanism           : Accumulates dW directly into SM register fragments during K-loop reduction,
                          applies AdamW update in-register, eliminating dW DRAM roundtrip (28B -> 22B/param).
  - Weight Matrix Diff  : 1.759175e-04 (Gate: < 1e-3) -> PASS
  - Momentum State Diff : 2.002344e-08 (Gate: < 1e-5) -> PASS
  - PyTorch Baseline    : 4.524 ms
  - Fused Kernel Latency: 1.633 ms
  - Training Speedup    : 2.77x on Tesla T4 -> PASS

